{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_backoffpolicy", "label": "BackoffPolicy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Entkoppelt von jedem konkreten Retry oder Supervisor, damit die Delay-Berechnung trivial testbar und wiederverwendbar ist. delayFor(restartCount) ist 0-basiert; der erste Retry uebergibt 0.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_exponentialbackoff", "label": "exponentialBackoff", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "min x 2^n gecappt auf max. Exponentiell, weil ein fehlschlagendes Upstream Zeit zum Erholen braucht; das Cappen bei max verhindert pathologisch lange Wartezeiten nach vielen Fehlern. Die bessere Wahl fuer Recovery.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_linearbackoff", "label": "linearBackoff", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "min + step x n gecappt auf max. Nische: begrenztes statt exponentielles Wachstum. Besser fuer Steady-State-Adaption (Poll-Kadenz, self-rate-limiting Producer), wo die Wachstumsrate der Wartezeit die akzeptable Last matcht.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_jitter", "label": "Jitter (randomFactor)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Wenn N Clients mit demselben Delay retrien, synchronisieren sie ihren naechsten Versuch zu einer donnernden Herde. +/-20 % Rauschen streut die Retries in der Zeit. randomFactor ausserhalb [0,1] wird abgelehnt, weil 1.0 bereits 'null bis doppeltes Delay' bedeutet und hoehere Werte nach dem Jitter auf 0 gefloort wuerden.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_random_injection", "label": "random-Override fuer Determinismus", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Beide Policies akzeptieren ein optionales random: () => number. Die Nichtdeterminismus-Quelle injizieren und festnageln macht delayFor(n) in Tests reproduzierbar; ein linearer Kongruenzgenerator reicht dafuer, in Produktion bleibt Math.random.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_retry_budget", "label": "Retry-Budget", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Die Policy cappt sauber bei maxMs, aber ein Aufrufer, der 5 Minuten zwischen Versuchen wartet, ist von 'transientem Fehler' zu 'totem Upstream' gewandert. Backoff mit einem Cap auf Gesamt-Versuche oder Gesamt-Zeit paaren und einen permanenten Fehler an einen Higher-Level-Alert surfacen.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_fibonaccibackoff", "label": "fibonacciBackoff (eigene Policy)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Beispiel fuer eine selbst implementierte BackoffPolicy; via die policy-Option an BackoffSupervisor uebergeben ueberschreibt sie das Default-Exponential-Wachstum.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_exponentialbackoff", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_backoffpolicy", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_linearbackoff", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_backoffpolicy", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_fibonaccibackoff", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_backoffpolicy", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_jitter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_exponentialbackoff", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_jitter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_linearbackoff", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_random_injection", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_jitter", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_retry_budget", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_backoffpolicy", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_backoffpolicy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}